{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqsVEuV6iBirJccFBGzuxN","type":"tool_result","content":"# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n----\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Ruta Cerámica · clases y taller</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Ruta Cerámica</h1>\n<p>Clases de torno y modelado en Villa Crespo.</p>\n<div id=\"booking\"></div>\n<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n----\n// Class booking widget: shows the next slots and a WhatsApp link.\n(function () {\n  var slots = [\n    { day: \"sábado\", time: \"10:00\", seats: 2 },\n    { day: \"martes\", time: \"18:30\", seats: 4 }\n  ];\n  var root = document.getElementById(\"booking\");\n  if (!root) return;\n  var html = \"<h2>Próximas clases</h2><ul>\";\n  slots.forEach(function (s) {\n    html += \"<li>\" + s.day + \" \" + s.time + \" · \" + s.seats + \" lugares</li>\";\n  });\n  html += \"</ul><a href='https://wa.me/5491100000000?text=Hola'><button>Reservar por WhatsApp</button></a>\";\n  root.innerHTML = html;\n})();\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\n<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58bd5be8-efdc-48a2-8814-897d0d714caf","uuid":"9121fac7-eca7-4528-9ab8-35899a0a1cc6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:02:12.394Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n----\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Ruta Cerámica · clases y taller</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Ruta Cerámica</h1>\n<p>Clases de torno y modelado en Villa Crespo.</p>\n<div id=\"booking\"></div>\n<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n----\n// Class booking widget: shows the next slots and a WhatsApp link.\n(function () {\n  var slots = [\n    { day: \"sábado\", time: \"10:00\", seats: 2 },\n    { day: \"martes\", time: \"18:30\", seats: 4 }\n  ];\n  var root = document.getElementById(\"booking\");\n  if (!root) return;\n  var html = \"<h2>Próximas clases</h2><ul>\";\n  slots.forEach(function (s) {\n    html += \"<li>\" + s.day + \" \" + s.time + \" · \" + s.seats + \" lugares</li>\";\n  });\n  html += \"</ul><a href='https://wa.me/5491100000000?text=Hola'><button>Reservar por WhatsApp</button></a>\";\n  root.innerHTML = html;\n})();\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\n<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LqsVEuV6iBirJccFBGzuxN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
