{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArPcxAaSRshoza91LYv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deploy now sets `Cache-Control` on every upload: `max-age=300` for HTML, CSS and JS, and `max-age=31536000` for `assets/`. I dry-ran the script with `aws` stubbed out, but I did not run it against S3 or CloudFront, so the live headers are still unchecked.\n\n- **`scripts/deploy.sh`**: re-uploads `src/` with the short policy (excluding `assets/`), then re-uploads `assets/` with the long policy, then runs `aws s3 sync --delete` to remove deleted files, then invalidates CloudFront as before. Re-uploading matters because `sync` alone skips unchanged files, so existing objects would never get the header.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: what changed, which parts of the colleague's note applied, the choices I made, and the `curl -sI` checks to run after your next deploy.\n\nDecisions you may want to revisit:\n- **CSS is on the short policy.** You didn't say, and it's not under `assets/`.\n- **Assets are cached for a year without renaming.** A changed `logo.png` won't reach returning visitors until the cache expires, so rename changed assets.\n- **Content-Type is left to the AWS CLI** to guess from each file's extension, rather than set per file type. The `curl` checks in `ANSWER.md` will show if the guess is wrong.\n- **The README's \"Known problem\" section is unchanged** and now describes a fixed issue. Update it once the deploy is confirmed.\n\nNothing was deployed or sent anywhere external."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_read_input_tokens":30808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use